# Cloudflare Pages response headers.

# Content-Security-Policy is in Report-Only mode: nothing is blocked, the
# browser only logs violations to the DevTools console. Once a week of normal
# use shows no violations (GA4 after consent, Turnstile, booking form), rename
# the header to Content-Security-Policy to enforce it.
#
# The two sha256 values are the inline scripts: the GA4 Consent Mode block in
# every page's <head>, and the language picker on 404.html. If either is edited
# (e.g. in tools/render*.js), recompute the hash (DevTools prints the expected
# value in the violation message) or the script will be blocked once the
# policy is enforced. challenges.cloudflare.com is the Turnstile widget on the
# booking form; Pages already sends nosniff and referrer-policy.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-3RlUdMj05MKZamcN+QITuroH1pyEgYDQNKTD4BuGIDY=' 'sha256-au50U4dZ32jCdgxcEhkE4pZ43Q6SR1n6QbhvuSdZU88=' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com; media-src 'self'; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

# Font files never change once shipped (a new version gets a new name), so they can be cached for a year.
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
